# What a customer's erasure (customers/redact) reaches in a store's mirror, and what it leaves.
#
# Rendered by TestTheErasurePolicyMatchesItsGolden from the generated model
# (integrations/shopify/generated/model.go) and the policy (integrations/shopify/erasure_fields.go).
# Never edited by hand: SHOPIFY_ERASURE_UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 go test ./integrations/shopify/ -run TestTheErasurePolicyMatchesItsGolden
# rewrites it, and its diff is the review.
#
# REACH. The scope starts at the customer's row and the orders the request names, and grows to a fixed
# point by these links and no other:
#   child of X              the row hangs from an in-scope row of X by the model's parent link
#   gid field F naming X    the row holds an in-scope row of X's gid as the whole value of its gid field F.
#                           Every gid field is such a link unless its line below says NOT A LINK. One of
#                           them is a link "from a deleted row only": it is followed from a row whose
#                           newest version is a tombstone, and from no other
#   the customer inside object F
#                           the row holds an in-scope customer's gid as an id inside its object F, and F
#                           is one of the few objects that say who a row is for. Her gid inside any other
#                           object, or as a free value anywhere (a custom attribute, a note, a message in
#                           that same object), is not a link: nothing is matched by value
# A list of references is not a link, and neither is an object that only refers to the customer (a
# metaobject's fields): in a row that is not in scope the entry that names her is taken out -- an entry
# that holds her gid as a whole value anywhere inside it -- and nothing else in the row changes.
#
# A ROW IS DECIDED ON WHAT IT IS NOW. A row is in scope, with everything that hangs from it, when its
# NEWEST version holds a link; the data request exports exactly those rows, each at its newest version.
# An OLDER version that holds the customer's gid in a link field, on a row whose newest version does not
# (an order since moved to another person), is scrubbed by itself: that version only, not the row's
# newest version and not what hangs from the row.
#
# AN ORDER THE REQUEST NAMES is a seed only when its newest version names the customer or names no
# customer. One that names another customer now is that person's: it is decided as a row that moved.
#
# A DELETED CUSTOMER ROW WHOSE LAST ORDER IS IN SCOPE is scrubbed BY ITSELF: nothing is reached from it
# (not its orders, not what names it) and it is never in an export. It may be a record merged into
# the customer, or another deleted person whose stale pointer names an order that is hers now.
#
# TWO THINGS AN ERASURE DOES NOT REACH, accepted in writing:
#   - a row that carries the person only by an email address, with no customer on it: a guest's
#     abandoned checkout
#   - the buyer's message inside a gift card another person holds: the card is its holder's
#
# FIELDS. Every version of a row in scope is rewritten. The structural fields are never touched:
#   storeId, gid, updatedAt, versionSource, syncedAt, versionReadAt, deleted, parentGid, accountId
# Every other field, and any key the model does not know, is decided below:
#   kept by kind            a gid, a list of references, an enum, or a scalar whose Admin type is one of:
#                           BigInt (an integer), Boolean (a boolean), Date (a date),
#                           DateTime (a date-time), Decimal (a decimal), Float (a float), ID (an ID),
#                           Int (an integer), Money (a money amount),
#                           UnsignedInt64 (an unsigned 64-bit number)
#   kept by the list        on the keep-list of erasure_fields.go, with the reason it describes the sale
#   scrubbed                everything else: a string of free text becomes "[redacted]", a list becomes [], and
#                           the key of anything else is removed (an object, a number, a boolean, an enum, and a
#                           string that is a date, a number or a reference), so a typed read answers null, a reader
#                           of dates never meets the marker, and the mirror can write the row again
#   scrubbed although kept by kind
#                           the person's own, on a row that is not her customer row; each says why
#   kept by the list; scrubbed on a custom item
#                           the one decision that looks at a row's values: a line item (orderLineItem) with no
#                           productGid is a custom item, whose titles and SKU are what a person typed. It is
#                           decided version by version
# The scalar Admin types the model holds that are not kept by kind:
#   CountryCode, CurrencyCode, HTML, JSON, LanguageCode, OrderTransactionErrorCode,
#   ShopifyPaymentsTransactionType, String, URL
# The columns are the field, its kind, its Admin type and the decision. A kept object or list is followed by
# what it holds.

concept abandonedCheckout (AbandonedCheckout)
  reach: gid field customerGid naming customer
  abandonedCheckoutUrl                     scalar      URL                                scrubbed: becomes "[redacted]"
  billingAddress                           object      MailingAddress                     scrubbed: the key is removed
  completedAt                              scalar      DateTime                           kept by kind: a date-time
  customAttributes                         objectList  Attribute                          scrubbed: becomes []
  customerGid                              gid         Customer                           kept by kind: a reference to another row; a link: a row that names an in-scope customer here is in scope
  defaultCursor                            scalar      String                             scrubbed: becomes "[redacted]"
  discountCodes                            scalarList  String                             kept by the list: the discount codes used on the sale
  name                                     scalar      String                             kept by the list: the checkout's number
  note                                     scalar      String                             scrubbed: becomes "[redacted]"
  shippingAddress                          object      MailingAddress                     scrubbed: the key is removed
  sourceCreatedAt                          scalar      DateTime                           kept by kind: a date-time
  subtotalPriceSet                         object      MoneyBag                           kept by the list: an amount of the sale
  taxLines                                 objectList  TaxLine                            kept by the list: tax lines: titles, rates and amounts
      holds { channelLiable priceSet { shopMoney { amount currencyCode } presentmentMoney { amount currencyCode } } rate ratePercentage source title }
  taxesIncluded                            scalar      Boolean                            kept by kind: a boolean
  totalDiscountSet                         object      MoneyBag                           kept by the list: an amount of the sale
  totalDutiesSet                           object      MoneyBag                           kept by the list: an amount of the sale
  totalLineItemsPriceSet                   object      MoneyBag                           kept by the list: an amount of the sale
  totalPriceSet                            object      MoneyBag                           kept by the list: an amount of the sale
  totalTaxSet                              object      MoneyBag                           kept by the list: an amount of the sale

